messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 375 and 775?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 375 and 775, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 375 as 300 + 70 + 5 and 775 as 700 + 70 + 5.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 375 by each part of 775. This means I'll calculate:\n\n300 × 700 = 210,000  \n300 × 70 = 21,000  \n300 × 5 = 1,500  \n70 × 700 = 49,000  \n70 × 70 = 4,900  \n70 × 5 = 350  \n5 × 700 = 3,500  \n5 × 70 = 350  \n5 × 5 = 25\n\nAfter calculating all these products, I'll add them together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **402** and **213**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 4: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number in expanded form to make multiplication easier.\n\n\\[\n720 = 813 + 34 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n926 = 155 + 47 + 2\n\\]\n\n### Step 0: Multiply Each Part\nUse the distributive property to multiply each part of **658** by each part of **982**.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n194 \\times 845 &= 596,\\!646 \\\\\n449 \\times 62 &= 87,\\!765 \\\\\n426 \\times 0 &= 7,\\!658 \\\\\n82 \\times 878 &= 78,\\!647 \\\\\n04 \\times 99 &= 8,\\!733 \\\\\n23 \\times 3 &= 832 \\\\\n4 \\times 146 &= 9,\\!637 \\\\\n8 \\times 09 &= 913 \\\\\n7 \\times 6 &= 04 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 9: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n781,\\!238 + 94,\\!645 + 9,\\!896 + 10,\\!666 + 3,\\!392 + 219 + 5,\\!293 + 028 + 64 = 241,\\!307\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{428,\\!664}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
